From 60ba1fba59be03cb7c07bba48c995f3414109e19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:16:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 316/316] player.c -- a stream repaints the artwork square, and
 says what it is

Two faults, both found by looking at the panel, and neither of which
fifteen patches of log reading could have shown.

**play_stream() was not consuming s_repaint_art at all.** That flag is
set by every screen drawn over the artwork -- the chooser, the settings
panel, the sleep page -- and consumed in three places: twice in
play_file()'s decode loop and once in the idle branch of player_loop().
play_stream() is beside play_file() and inherited none of them, so a
chooser dismissed during a stream left its file listing on screen above
the bar for as long as the stream ran.

That is 0204's amplifier again -- a postcondition play_file() owns and
play_stream() needs -- and it is the third time "beside play_file()" has
cost exactly one of these per screen element. It is still the right
structure; this is its price, and the price is one patch per element
rather than one bug per track.

**And the square was black, which this project already decided is the
wrong answer.** ui_show_art_info()'s own note says black reads as a
cover that has not arrived rather than one that does not exist, and that
what belongs there instead is the thing the source can always say about
itself. That argument was written for a file with no picture in it and
holds unchanged for a stream; a stream simply never got the call.

show_stream_card() puts the station on top, then the codec, then the
rate -- largest to smallest, the same hierarchy the format card uses for
a file. Mono is named and stereo is not: stereo is the expectation, and
WUOM being mono is the sort of thing that otherwise reads as a fault in
the player.

Drawn with whatever is known. Before the first frame there is no codec
and no rate and the card is just the station name, which is honest;
waiting for the numbers would leave the square black for the three
seconds this exists to fill. Redrawn from the card rather than through
load_track_visuals(), which wants a path a stream does not have.

Reported from the panel as "nothing album-art-wise" and "with no art the
radio list is never blacked out when closing the menu".
---
 main/player.c | 83 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 83 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main/player.c b/main/player.c
index ffde394..59bbec4 100644
--- a/main/player.c
+++ b/main/player.c
@@ -8758,6 +8758,58 @@ static void clear_play_screen(void)
 /* play_stream() -- a live stream, beside play_file() and not inside it */
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 
+/*
+ * What goes in the artwork square while a stream plays.
+ *
+ * A stream has no cover and `ui_clear_art()` leaves 720x720 of black,
+ * which this project has already decided is the wrong answer -- it is
+ * the note on ui_show_art_info(): black reads as a cover that has not
+ * arrived rather than one that does not exist, and what goes there
+ * instead is the thing the source can always say about itself. That
+ * argument was written for a file with no picture in it and applies
+ * unchanged here; a stream simply never got the call.
+ *
+ * The station on top because it is the thing chosen, then the format,
+ * then the rate -- largest to smallest, the same hierarchy the format
+ * card uses for a file.
+ *
+ * Called with whatever is known. Before the first frame the codec and
+ * the rate are not, and the lines are simply shorter: a card that says
+ * only the station name is honest, and waiting for the numbers would
+ * leave the square black for the three seconds this exists to fill.
+ */
+static void show_stream_card(uint32_t rate, int chans, int kbps)
+{
+    char fmt[48];
+    char det[48];
+    const char *lines[3];
+    int n = 0;
+
+    lines[n++] = s_stream_top[0] ? s_stream_top : "Radio";
+
+    const stream_codec_t c = netdec_codec();
+    if (c != STREAM_CODEC_NONE) {
+        snprintf(fmt, sizeof(fmt), "%s", stream_codec_name(c));
+        lines[n++] = fmt;
+    }
+
+    if (rate > 0) {
+        /* Mono is worth saying and stereo is not: stereo is the
+         * expectation, and WUOM being mono is the sort of thing that
+         * otherwise reads as a fault in the player. */
+        if (kbps > 0) {
+            snprintf(det, sizeof(det), "%" PRIu32 " Hz  %s  %d kbit/s",
+                     rate, chans == 1 ? "mono" : "stereo", kbps);
+        } else {
+            snprintf(det, sizeof(det), "%" PRIu32 " Hz  %s",
+                     rate, chans == 1 ? "mono" : "stereo");
+        }
+        lines[n++] = det;
+    }
+
+    ui_show_art_info(lines, n);
+}
+
